7 transformer orders by about 40% and resize its Q1 2027 tender (n5.d5). That shows equity funding failed for the largest buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, and the plan was scaled back as a result.\n- **Wider market:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size in Q3 (n5.d5). The credit report says \"equity markets have been less receptive\" (n5.d4).\n- **Norvane Utilities:** It priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (n5.d4). So debt is still open to at least some issuers, even though utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Debt is the more workable route.\n\n**Implication:** Plans that depend on equity are likely to be delayed or shrunk. Pellham's 40% cut in transformer orders is the clearest example. Debt markets are the better route, and my sibling nodes n3 and n5 are covering that question.\n\n**Gaps:** I did not find the 2027 capex amounts. The documents point to a utility tender calendar and Pellham's market statement, and I couldn't find either. So I can't say how large the equity shortfall is.","ttft_ms":2176,"type":"result","duration_ms":20981,"uuid":"e2ccdbc0-791c-4dea-8a47-185a97a6677f","ttft_stream_ms":1726,"time_to_request_ms":240,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":31,"system_prompt":17,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":11,"input_attachments":32,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":4,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":8,"init_message":20,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":11,"message_prep":11,"model_config_wait":6,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":23,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":8,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":7,"client_creation":12,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":110,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":75,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":198,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":124,"process_rss_mib_result":198,"process_anon_mib_result":117,"process_peak_rss_mib":203,"process_cpu_ms_turn":546,"process_wa